WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.250
By now we are aware of almost all the changes
that occur during puberty in

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.740
both boys and girls.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.619
So can you tell me which is the most important
of all

00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:15.619
changes?

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:16.619
Yes!

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:20.029
It is the development of reproductive organs.

00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:25.590
The stage of sexual maturation is what defines
puberty in true sense.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.500
And what
do we mean by this?

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.530
This means that the individual is now physically
capable

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.290
of reproduction.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:37.240
So are we saying that both males and females
are capable of reproduction with

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.500
the onset of puberty?

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.170
Absolutely!

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.510
And that would mean that they can
reproduce anytime throughout their life right?

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.970
Absolutely NOT!

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.430
Why not?

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:51.260
The basic reason for this is that the case
of males

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:55.750
and females is different when it comes to
the reproductive span.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.700
And why is
this different?

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.120
This is what we need to answer in this video
that deals with the concept of

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.690
REPRODUCTIVE PHASE.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.350
Now what exactly do we mean by this?

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.649
Let us understand the two words.

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:13.109
REPRODUCTIVE here means the process of reproduction.

00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:15.020
And Phase means
the time period.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.429
So are we saying that individuals are capable
of reproduction

00:01:19.429 --> 00:01:21.789
only for some period of time?

00:01:21.789 --> 00:01:22.920
Yes!

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:26.459
And this is applicable only in case of
Females.

00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:27.459
But why so?

00:01:27.459 --> 00:01:28.880
Let me explain.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.959
In case of males, development of testes causes
production of gametes, that is

00:01:34.959 --> 00:01:36.090
sperms.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.380
And this process once started, does not terminate
throughout the

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.340
male’s life.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.819
Only the sperms produced can decrease in count
with age.

00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:49.240
However, the ability to reproduce still remains
the same.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:53.240
But the case of females is completely different.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:56.500
Females cannot reproduce
throughout their lives.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.560
The term Reproductive phase holds true in
their case.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.249
And why is it so?

00:02:03.249 --> 00:02:07.919
Well the simplest answer to this question
is the process of OVULATION!

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.060
Yes!

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.620
Can you guess from the name, what is ovulation?

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:18.050
It is the process of release of
ova from the ovaries.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:22.430
Now you may wonder how the process can be
an answer to this question.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.470
It’s simple!

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:28.300
We know that reproduction requires an egg
cell as the female

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.460
gamete.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.270
And if ovulation is the release of egg cells,
then that means

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:38.220
reproduction will be possible only when egg
cells are released.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.530
But do you
know that in every female individual, the

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.510
number of egg follicles in the ovaries
is fixed?

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.290
That means the ovaries will have fixed number
of immature egg cells

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.230
stored inside them since the beginning.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:58.480
However, only on the onset of puberty,
the egg cells are released one after the other.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.610
So don’t you think the capacity of reproduction
will begin when the first egg

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.900
cell will be released by the ovary?

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:04.900
Yes!

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:11.090
And it will obviously stop when the
number of egg cells will come to an end!

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:15.340
This phase is nothing but the reproductive
phase in females.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:20.650
The beginning and end of this important phase
are given scientific names.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.750
The commencing point is called as MENARCHE.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:28.800
So can we say a girl
experiences Menarche when she steps into puberty?

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.050
Yes!

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.800
And the occurrence
differs from one female to the other.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:39.560
However the average age range to expect
Menarche is around twelve to fourteen years.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:44.530
Also, the time when it
terminates is called MENOPAUSE!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.040
This time is also different in females.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.760
But the
average period of age is between forty five

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.850
to fifty years.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:57.100
Let us just imagine that one of the ovaries
has released an egg cell.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.900
It goes
straight to the fallopian tube and then moves

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.410
further.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:05.120
Now if this egg gets
fertilised, then the foetus will need a proper

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.569
location for placental attachment
right?

00:04:08.569 --> 00:04:12.490
For this, a proper thick cushion layer made
up of cells needs to be

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:15.490
formed inside the uterus.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:19.579
We know this layer is called the ENDOMETRIUM.

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:23.830
But how will the reproductive tract know whether
fertilisation is going to occur

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.350
or not?

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:30.250
How will it form the Endometrium all of a
sudden if fertilisation occurs?

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:35.569
The natural tendency of our body is to be
prepared for every possibility!

00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:38.729
So in
this case too, our body makes the necessary

00:04:38.729 --> 00:04:39.729
preparations.

00:04:39.729 --> 00:04:44.050
When the ovum is
released from either of the ovaries, many

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.969
hormones work in co-ordination to
get the endometrial layer ready.

00:04:48.969 --> 00:04:54.759
In case fertilisation occurs, the foetus will
have a proper location for placental attachment.

00:04:54.759 --> 00:05:00.470
Wait a second… we said if fertilisation
occurs!

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.960
What if it doesn’t?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.530
In that case
the ovum will come out of the body through

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.900
the vagina.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:06.900
And what will happen

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.620
to the endometrium?

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:12.229
Astonishingly, the layer also collapses and
gets out of the

00:05:12.229 --> 00:05:13.499
body through the vagina.

00:05:13.499 --> 00:05:19.259
As a result of this, for almost four to five
days every month, a female

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:21.919
experiences a bleeding phase.

00:05:21.919 --> 00:05:26.729
The bleeding is through the vagina and it
contains the unfertilised ovum, the cells

00:05:26.729 --> 00:05:30.360
of endometrium and blood of course!

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.539
This is called as the MENSTRUAL FLUID.

00:05:32.539 --> 00:05:37.279
And the process is referred to as
Menstruation.

00:05:37.279 --> 00:05:41.919
Did you notice I mentioned that the bleeding
phase is four to five days EVERY

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:42.919
MONTH?

00:05:42.919 --> 00:05:45.789
Why did I say every month?

00:05:45.789 --> 00:05:50.590
That is because the entire process occurs
in a cyclic manner that lasts for

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:52.960
twenty eight to thirty days.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.629
The ovulation and building up of the endometrium,
and then followed by this will be collapsing

00:05:58.629 --> 00:06:03.139
of endometrium in case
fertilisation does not occur.

00:06:03.139 --> 00:06:05.349
This will give rise to the discharge of the
menstrual

00:06:05.349 --> 00:06:07.080
fluid through the vagina.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:12.000
Don’t you think this entire cycle will also
have a scientific name?

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.339
Of course!

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.639
It is
called the MENSTRUAL CYCLE.

00:06:15.639 --> 00:06:18.509
So the Menstrual cycle is almost a twenty
eight

00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:23.839
to thirty day cycle out of which the bleeding
phase lasts for four to five days.

00:06:23.839 --> 00:06:29.479
In a nutshell, the reproductive ability is
obtained by individuals with the onset

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:31.009
of puberty.

00:06:31.009 --> 00:06:33.860
In males, it lasts till they’re alive.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:38.169
However, in females the
reproductive phase is marked by the menarche,

00:06:38.169 --> 00:06:39.169
and concluded by menopause.

00:06:39.169 --> 00:06:46.050
The time period in between is where the body
undergoes the menstrual cycle.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:51.099
The reproductive capacity of females is only
found during this phase.

00:06:51.099 --> 00:06:55.419
So we have talked about the process that happens
when fertilisation does not

00:06:55.419 --> 00:06:56.919
take place.

00:06:56.919 --> 00:06:59.770
But what if fertilisation occurs?

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.759
Do we know whether it’ll be a boy or a girl?

00:07:02.759 --> 00:07:08.889
Let us learn about the concept of
SEX DETERMINATION in the next video!

